From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:41:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 347/353] mmc: sdhci-pci-gli: GL9755: restore the vendor
 configuration after power loss

The GL9755's vendor configuration (gl9755_hw_setting(): the Apple card
detect and write protect inversion, the PLL, SerDes and power-saving
settings) lives in registers a fundamental reset clears. Probe applies
it, and so does runtime resume; system resume does not, as the reader
keeps its power across a sleep everywhere else.

A T8132 deep sleep powers the J604's APCIe block down, and the reader
with it. It then comes back with card detect no longer inverted, so a
card in the slot reads as absent and is dropped right after the wake,
and an empty slot reads as a card.

Apply the vendor configuration again on a resume via firmware, before
the host resumes. A sleep that keeps power (suspend-to-idle) is
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
index 0a3eb26daf..21cca237d1 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include "sdhci.h"
 #include "sdhci-cqhci.h"
 #include "sdhci-pci.h"
@@ -1966,6 +1967,20 @@ static int sdhci_pci_gli_resume(struct sdhci_pci_chip *chip)
 	return sdhci_pci_resume_host(chip);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A system sleep that cut the reader's power (a T8132 deep sleep powers the
+ * APCIe block down) resets its vendor configuration, card detect inversion
+ * included, as at power-on: apply it again, as probe and runtime resume do.
+ * A sleep that keeps power (suspend-to-idle) does not resume via firmware.
+ */
+static int gl9755_resume(struct sdhci_pci_chip *chip)
+{
+	if (pm_resume_via_firmware())
+		gl9755_hw_setting(chip->slots[0]);
+
+	return sdhci_pci_gli_resume(chip);
+}
+
 static int gl9763e_resume(struct sdhci_pci_chip *chip)
 {
 	struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot = chip->slots[0];
@@ -2091,7 +2106,7 @@ const struct sdhci_pci_fixes sdhci_gl9755 = {
 	.remove_host	= sdhci_pci_uhs2_remove_host,
 	.ops            = &sdhci_gl9755_ops,
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
-	.resume         = sdhci_pci_gli_resume,
+	.resume         = gl9755_resume,
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
 	/* Used only when gl9755_runtime_pm allows runtime PM at probe */
-- 
